  "live_records": {
    "q-127734": {
      "dom_id": "step-q127734",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Calculate ${lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t),$ if $f(t)=⟨{e}^{t-2},\\,\\sqrt{6-t},\\,\\frac{3}{t+2}⟩.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, recall that\n\n$$\n{lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)=⟨{lim}_{t\\to 2}{e}^{t-2},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\sqrt{6-t},\\,{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{3}{t+2}⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the limits one by one.\n\n- For the first component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}{e}^{t-2} & ={e}^{2-2} \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the second component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\sqrt{6-t} & =\\sqrt{6-2} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For the third component, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 2}\\frac{3}{t+2} & =\\frac{3}{2+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, ${lim}_{t\\to 2}f(t)=⟨1,2,\\frac{3}{4}⟩.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
