    "q-32973": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32973",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Find ${lim}_{t\\to 0}[3f(t)-g(t)]$ given that\n$f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,{t}^{2}-2,\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\ g(t) & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\sqrt{t}+\\sqrt{2},2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}({t}^{2}-2),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\frac{t-3}{{t}^{2}+1})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡0,{0}^{2}-2,\\frac{0-3}{{0}^{2}+1}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,-3⟩ \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) & =⟨{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(\\sqrt{t}+\\sqrt{2}),\\,{lim}_{t\\to 0}(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡0,\\sqrt{0}+\\sqrt{2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\sqrt{2},2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to 0}[3f(t)-g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to 0}3f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =3{lim}_{t\\to 0}f(t)-{lim}_{t\\to 0}g(t) \\\\  & =3⟨1,-2,-3⟩-⟨0,\\sqrt{2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6,-9⟩-⟨0,\\sqrt{2},2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3-0,-6-\\sqrt{2},-9-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,-6-\\sqrt{2},-11⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
