    "q-32274": {
      "dom_id": "step-q32274",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Find the limit ${lim}_{t\\to \\pi }[f(t)\\cdot g(t)]$ given that $f(t)$ and $g(t)$ are defined as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t \\\\ 1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ \\frac{4t}{\\pi }\\end{aligned}],\\,g(t)=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t \\\\ 2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the limit of each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\frac{4t}{\\pi })\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\pi  \\\\ 1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ \\frac{4\\pi }{\\pi }\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }g(t) & =[\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡t) \\\\ {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }\\,(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\ (2+\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\pi ) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi \\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use properties of limits to calculate the final result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{t\\to \\pi }[f(t)\\cdot g(t)] & ={lim}_{t\\to \\pi }f(t)\\cdot {lim}_{t\\to \\pi }g(t) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =0\\cdot (-1)+0\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-1) \\\\  & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
